## Design Philosophy

HeroUI v3 follows 10 core principles that guide every implementation decision:

1. **Accessibility First** - Every component is keyboard navigable and screen reader friendly
2. **Composable Architecture** - Build complex UIs from simple, reusable parts
3. **Semantic Intent** - Components express purpose, not just appearance
4. **Progressive Disclosure** - Reveal complexity gradually as needed
5. **Type Safety** - Full TypeScript support with comprehensive types
6. **Separation of Concerns** - Logic, styling, and behavior are cleanly separated
7. **Predictable Behavior** - Consistent patterns across all components
8. **Performance Optimized** - Minimal runtime overhead, tree-shakeable
9. **Framework Flexibility** - React today, more frameworks tomorrow
10. **AI-Ready Design** - Structured for LLM understanding and generation

## MCP Tools Workflow

### Essential Tool Chain for Development

Always follow this workflow when implementing HeroUI components:

```javascript
// Note: This MCP only supports HeroUI React components (always uses latest version)

// Step 1: Check available components
await mcp.list_components();
// No parameters needed - returns all components with latest version

// Step 2: Get complete component documentation
const info = await mcp.get_component_info({
  component: "Card", // Must be one of the available components
});
// Returns: description, anatomy, props, examples, styling (latest version)

// Step 3: Get TypeScript prop types
const props = await mcp.get_component_props({
  component: "Card",
});

// Step 4: Get implementation examples
const examples = await mcp.get_component_examples({
  component: "Card",
});

// Step 5: Get theme variables for customization
const theme = await mcp.get_theme_info({
  theme: "default",
  mode: "both", // light, dark, or both
  category: "colors", // colors, spacing, typography, etc.
});
```

### When to Use Each Tool

| Tool                          | Use Case                                        | Example Query                          |
| ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| `list_components`             | Starting any project, checking what's available | "What components does HeroUI provide?" |
| `get_component_info`          | Before using ANY component                      | "How do I use the Card component?"     |
| `get_component_props`         | Type checking, prop validation                  | "What props does Button accept?"       |
| `get_component_examples`      | Implementation patterns                         | "Show me Card examples"                |
| `get_component_source_code`   | View React/TypeScript source code               | "Show me Button source code"           |
| `get_component_source_styles` | View CSS styles                                 | "Show me Card styles"                  |
| `get_theme_info`              | Customization, theming                          | "What are the color variables?"        |

### Common Workflows

#### Implementing a New Component

```typescript
// WORKFLOW: Card Implementation
// Note: This MCP only supports HeroUI React components (always uses latest version)

// 1. Check it exists
const components = await list_components();

// 2. Get full documentation
const cardInfo = await get_component_info({
  component: "Card", // Must be one of the available components
});

// 3. Review anatomy (CRITICAL for compound components)
console.log(cardInfo.anatomy);
// Output: ["Card", "Card.Image", "Card.Header", "Card.Title", "Card.Description", "Card.Content", "Card.Footer"]

// 4. Get examples for patterns
const examples = await get_component_examples({
  component: "Card",
});

// 5. Implement with correct structure
```

## Component Architecture

### Compound Components Pattern

**CRITICAL:** HeroUI v3 uses compound components. Never use flat prop patterns.

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Compound components with anatomy
<Card>
  <Card.Image src="/hero.jpg" alt="Hero image" />
  <Card.Header>
    <Card.Title>Product Name</Card.Title>
    <Card.Description>Short description</Card.Description>
  </Card.Header>
  <Card.Content>
    <p>Main content goes here with full flexibility</p>
  </Card.Content>
  <Card.Footer>
    <Button variant="accent">Buy Now</Button>
    <Button variant="ghost">Learn More</Button>
  </Card.Footer>
</Card>

// ❌ WRONG - Flat props (not supported)
<Card
  title="Product Name"
  description="Short description"
  content="Main content"
  footer={<Button>Buy Now</Button>}
/>
```

## Styling System

### CSS Variables Architecture

HeroUI uses a three-layer CSS variable system. Always query with `get_theme_info`:

```css
/* Layer 1: Base Primitives */
--white: oklch(1 0 0);
--black: oklch(0 0 0);
--spacing-1: 0.25rem;
--radius-sm: 0.375rem;

/* Layer 2: Semantic Tokens */
--color-accent: oklch(0.7 0.25 260);
--color-success: oklch(0.65 0.2 140);
--color-danger: oklch(0.6 0.25 30);
--font-size-body: 1rem;

/* Layer 3: Calculated/Dynamic */
--color-accent-hover: oklch(0.65 0.25 260);
--shadow-card: 0 2px 8px oklch(0 0 0 / 0.1);
```

