## Framework-Agnostic Usage (BEM Classes)

When React isn't available, use @heroui/styles for styling:

```html
<!-- Include styles via CDN -->
<link
  href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@heroui/styles@3.0.0-alpha.33/dist/heroui.min.css"
  rel="stylesheet"
  crossorigin="anonymous"
/>

<!-- Button variants using BEM -->
<div class="flex gap-4 p-4">
  <button class="button button--accent button--md">Primary Action</button>
  <button class="button button--secondary button--md">Secondary</button>
  <button class="button button--danger button--md">Delete</button>
  <button class="button button--ghost button--md" disabled>Disabled</button>
</div>
```

**WARNING:** BEM classes provide styling only - no JavaScript behavior, keyboard navigation, or ARIA attributes. Use @heroui/react for full accessibility.

### Component Extension (Custom Variants)

```tsx
// Extending HeroUI components with custom variants
interface CustomButtonProps extends ButtonProps {
  variant?: "accent" | "gradient" | "neon";
  size?: "xs" | "sm" | "md" | "lg" | "xl";
}

const CustomButton = forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, CustomButtonProps>(
  ({variant = "accent", size = "md", className, ...props}, ref) => {
    const variantStyles = {
      gradient: "bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-500 to-pink-500 text-white",
      neon: "shadow-neon border-2 border-cyan-400 text-cyan-400",
    };

    const sizeStyles = {
      xs: "px-2 py-1 text-xs",
      xl: "px-8 py-4 text-xl",
    };

    return (
      <Button
        ref={ref}
        className={cn(variantStyles[variant], sizeStyles[size], className)}
        {...props}
      />
    );
  },
);
```

## Accessibility Best Practices

### Keyboard Navigation

All HeroUI React components include full keyboard support:

```tsx
// Components handle keyboard automatically
<Button
  onPress={handleAction} // Uses onPress, not onClick
  onKeyDown={(e) => {
    // Additional keyboard handling if needed
    if (e.key === "Enter" && e.ctrlKey) {
      handleSpecialAction();
    }
  }}
>
  Keyboard Accessible
</Button>
```

## Troubleshooting Guide

### Common Issues and Solutions

#### Component Not Rendering

```typescript
// PROBLEM: Component doesn't appear
<Card title="Test" />  // ❌ Wrong

// SOLUTION: Use compound components
<Card>  // ✅ Correct
  <Card.Header>
    <Card.Title>Test</Card.Title>
  </Card.Header>
</Card>

// DEBUGGING: Check component info
const info = await get_component_info({
  component: "Card" // This MCP only supports HeroUI React components
});
console.log(info.anatomy); // See required structure
```

#### Styling Not Applied

```typescript
// PROBLEM: Tailwind classes not working
// CHECK 1: Ensure Tailwind v4 is installed
npm list tailwindcss  // Should show v4.x.x

// CHECK 2: Verify config includes HeroUI
// index.css or global.css (Tailwind CSS v4)
@import "tailwindcss";

@import "@heroui/styles";


// CHECK 3: CSS variables loaded
const theme = await get_theme_info({
  category: "all"
});
// Apply missing variables
```

#### TypeScript Errors

```typescript
// PROBLEM: Type errors with props
// SOLUTION: Get correct types
const props = await get_component_props({
  component: "Button",
});

// Use generated types
import type {ButtonProps} from "@heroui/react";

interface CustomProps extends ButtonProps {
  // Your extensions
}
```

### Debugging Checklist

1. **Component Issues**
   - [ ] Used `get_component_info` to verify API?
   - [ ] Following compound component pattern?
   - [ ] Imported from correct package?

2. **Styling Issues**
   - [ ] Tailwind CSS v4 installed?
   - [ ] HeroUI plugin configured?
   - [ ] CSS variables defined?
   - [ ] Dark mode class applied correctly?

3. **Behavior Issues**
   - [ ] Using `onPress` instead of `onClick`?
   - [ ] ARIA attributes present?
   - [ ] Keyboard navigation working?

4. **Performance Issues**
   - [ ] Components memoized where needed?
   - [ ] Lazy loading implemented?
   - [ ] Unused components tree-shaken?

